Package: m6APrediction
Type: Package
Title: Predict m6A Sites from Sequence and Structural Features
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Zihan", family = "Su",
           email = "Zihan.Su2402@student.xjtlu.edu.cn",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a random forest classifier that predicts
    N6-methyladenosine (m6A) RNA modification sites from sequence and
    structural features. Candidate sites are described by GC content, RNA
    type, RNA region, exon length, distance to the nearest splice junction,
    evolutionary conservation and the five-nucleotide sequence context, and
    the package returns the predicted probability of m6A together with a
    binary status. A fitted model and a 100-row example feature table are
    bundled so that both exported functions run out of the box.
